hello and welcome to the new world  review your source for everything anime  or manga and today we're going to take  some time to talk about demon slayer or  more accurately what i've experienced of  it to this point so for quite some time  now people have been asking me to watch  and read demon slayer and make content  on it and while i can't promise that i  did decide to finally take the plunge  and my first impressions of the series  are pretty damn favorable actually to be  clear at the moment i'm 7 episodes into  the anime adaptation which is already a  very very good sign because usually if i  don't like or I'm feeling a bit about  something I will have dropped it and  forgotten about it by episode 5 at most  however in regards to Demon Slayer I  suspect I'll be picking up the pace and  devouring this very much as quickly as I  can  I was pretty hooked from the get-go  because it's always nice to see a dark  Shonen that isn't afraid to explore some  of the more grim aspects of life and I  especially appreciate the tone and  atmosphere set by the anime I think it's  done a wonderful job at creating a world  that is very familiar and yet radically  different which makes me all the more  keen to explore it further as for the  premise I quite like the brother-sister  dynamic going on here I mean it feels  like a very standard Shonen plot in some  ways The Reluctant here are called to  action by a tragedy and working towards  writing something you say this idea  explored in a million other series but  so far it's being done exceptionally  well here and I'm more than happy to be  on board for the ride  the main character Tonto is similarly  familiar he has a lot of classic Shonen  tropes going on like the inherited  special skill and the drive to push  oneself beyond standard human  limitations but at the same time he  brings a wonderful level of depth for a  protagonist and he's very easy to  empathize with and cheer for as a result  as for his sister and driving for snow  Zuko I can't really say have spent  enough time with her to form a proper  opinion I mean most of the time I've  known her she's been asleep and I'm  preparing myself for the potential that  that's how she'll spend most of the  series as well although I really hope  that's not the case at the moment I'd  say that she's simultaneously cute and  heartbreaking it's absolutely adorable  to see her do things like dig a hole to  rest in but shortly after that effect  wears off and the reality of her  situation very quickly sets in what I do  really like is that no Zuko seems to be  the more literal representation of a  core idea of the series which is the  bloodlines between humans and demons I  mean so far the series has gone to great  lengths to try and state how radically  opposed these two existences are and yet  most of what it's actually showing us  says the exact opposite Naza KO is the  prime example of that being at once  human and demon but it seems to be a  very common theme I mean in the most  recent episode I've seen I got quite a  shock when tonzura found  boyo whose dam I think is Mouzon cubits  ooh gee I don't know I haven't spent  enough time with him yet but I was  shocked that he had a human family you  know this figure who has been built up  to be the most evil existence we've seen  thus far  we're shown to be living a somewhat  peaceful life with the human family now  of course I have no idea how real any of  that is or whether or not he cares for  them at all but the point is that the  series is throwing that idea out there  it also does this rather nicely by  humanizing select demons in fact  actually I think that every major demon  that tandro has come across so far for  me has heard the humanizing moment the  most obvious one being the big fat arm  demon who even got a short flashback and  tandra went so far as to comfort him as  he died and I love that sort of stuff  because the series like this can really  run the risk of becoming very boring  very quickly through flight antagonists  especially when you're dealing with  demons because there's often no attempt  to try and make them anything more than  what they're perceived as which is  otherworldly killing for the fun of  killing beings demon slayer thus far has  done a very good job of actually making  me care about the primary demons we've  faced off against to the point where  it's often a shame when they do  eventually need to be killed so I'm very  interested to see where this goes in the  future and whether or not this line of  humanity and Amonte is going to be  blurred even more to the point where  it's completely flipped and there are  some humans out there who are more  monstrous than demons or even if there  are demons out there with more  protective human qualities I don't know  if I'm hoping for too much there from a  shounen series the Demon Slayer has  gotten off to a very solid start so my  imagination is sky-high and something  else that I love about the anime  specifically is the beautiful way in  which it depicts things like tandra a  sense of smell or his sword techniques  would the wonderfully stylized water I  mean I'm sure that's probably how its  depicted in the margaret's well but the  anime makes these scenes flow  phenomenally to the point where I  classify them as a class a visual feast  so I'm always excited when Tantra goes  into battle because I know that aside  from some great action I'll probably be  seeing some cool stylized water as well  furthermore the music is near-perfect  and absurdly important in contributing  to the atmosphere of the world for want  of a better explanation I'm horrible  with music but it feels deep as if it's  old and established like the world  itself and it adds that layer of  believability and immersion to any given  location or situation it's also pretty  hard to ignore the opening and ending  songs because you can never go wrong  with Lisa  I mean her opening was quite possibly  the only saving factor behind the first  sword out online series I think it was  called crossing field and you know just  thinking about it makes me want to  listen to it again I was also a huge fan  of what she did for the various fate  series so to have both an  opening and then ending from her here is  a real treat but yeah there's not a  whole lot more to say really at the  moment I don't have any major criticism  of the series I think it's moving at a  nice pace and giving our primary  characters the time they need to really  establish themselves before providing  too much of an extended cast which from  the opening I know is probably  inevitable and I do look forward to it  but right now I really am enjoying the  more small-scale character focus  actually just before I move away from  this something else I'm really enjoying  is the prominence of masks in the series  I am a huge fan of masks so suck kanji  was an instant favorite of mine as was  the bladesmith who arrived wearing the  clown mask he was a nice bit of fun as  well and it is good to note the Demon  Slayer despite its dark wanderings is  not devoid of humor there are nice  moments of laughter even if it's only a  small chuckle and I think that is very  necessary to break up the tone here and  there but that's about it for now I'm  going to win this video so that I can go  and continue watching the series and  I'll probably post a final thoughts  about it once the anime has concluded  and if it continues to hold my interest  and I'll probably move on to the manga  as well whatever the case exciting times  ahead and that pretty much does it for  my first impressions of Demon Slayer if  you enjoyed this video and the content  this channel produces in general then  please do consider donating to the new  ultra view patreon because the support  of all of your amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share or subscribe because it also helps  plot the channel an incredible amount  and if you'd like to join the fun at any  time then please do head over to my  discord server where a wide array of  shenanigan ori takes place on a daily  basis and finally please do comment with  your thoughts on Demon Slayer  this has been the new world review and  I'll see you next time  you  [Music]

